  "goodToKnow": "Der Tänzer (die Tänzerin) is a dancer: ein Balletttänzer, eine Profitänzerin. Many German teenagers take a Tanzkurs at a Tanzschule to learn ballroom dances before their Abiball (graduation ball). German dance has a strong modern tradition, from Pina Bausch's Tanztheater in Wuppertal to the Ausdruckstanz of the 1920s. From tanzen (to dance) and der Tanz. Note the umlaut. The plural is the same: die Tänzer."
